---
description: Implement proper consent management for data collection and processing
alwaysApply: true
---

consent-management:

- Obtain explicit consent before collecting personal data
- Provide granular consent options (not all-or-nothing)
- Make consent withdrawal as easy as giving consent
- Store consent records with timestamps
- Re-request consent when purposes change
- Implement consent for cookies and tracking
- Provide clear privacy notices before consent
- Never use pre-checked boxes for consent

Consent requirements:
- Must be freely given, specific, informed, and unambiguous
- Clear affirmative action required (opt-in, not opt-out)
- Separate consent for different processing purposes
- Easy withdrawal mechanism
- Documented consent records

Good implementation:
```javascript
// Granular consent
const consentForm = {
  essential: true, // Required for service
  analytics: false, // User choice
  marketing: false, // User choice
  thirdParty: false // User choice
};

await db.consents.create({
  userId,
  consents: consentForm,
  timestamp: new Date(),
  ipAddress: req.ip
});

// Easy withdrawal
async function withdrawConsent(userId, consentType) {
  await db.consents.update(userId, {
    [consentType]: false,
    withdrawnAt: new Date()
  });
  await stopProcessing(userId, consentType);
}
```

Bad practices:
```javascript
// Pre-checked consent
<input type="checkbox" checked> Accept all

// No consent record
// Just start collecting data

// No withdrawal mechanism
```
